# MANDATORY STOP POINTS V1.2

> **Purpose**: Enforce the 2 user checkpoints in the lean flow, codify constitutional principles, prevent autopilot, define forbidden/required phrases.
>
> **v1.1 change**: Reduced from 8 stop points to 2. The remaining 6 dimensions (project card, status, summary, completed/in-progress, ask/attention, metrics) are now folded into the **single Phase 1 batch** so the user reviews everything once instead of seven times.
>
> **v1.2 change**: Stop points unchanged (still 2). Underlying script enforcement reduced from 12 → 6 validators; the LLM now performs date/recipient/section-order/forbidden-header/fresh-email checks natively in its `<thinking>` block. Bundle reduced from 6 → 4 files (plain-text preview + gap list now rendered inline in chat).

---

## 2 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

Each stop point is a hard gate. Agent MUST NOT proceed without explicit user response.

| # | Name | Phase | What the User Decides | Why Human Judgment Matters |
|---|------|-------|------------------------|-----------------------------|
| **SP1** | Updates Batch Reply | 1 | Provides leaves/holidays, Jira paste or metric description, free-form section updates/additions/removals; may override any inferred field | Even with strong reference inference, the user owns this week's actual updates and the leaves data the agent cannot know |
| **SP2** | Final Draft Approval | 2 | Approves the full assembled draft (subject + body + HTML + text + validation summary + gap report); may request edits or abort | Last line of defense before the user sends — final inspection covers HTML, plain text, subject line, every metric, every bullet |

**Non-negotiable:** Agent is FORBIDDEN to advance past either stop point without an explicit user response.

**What's NOT a stop point** (silent in v1.1):
- Phase 0 ingest — runs without prompting (parser confidence noted internally)
- Per-section approvals — folded into the SP1 batch
- Validation report — runs silently in Phase 2 background; only failures surface at SP2
- Sycophancy nudge — appears inline in SP1 batch, not as its own stop

