## FORBIDDEN PHRASES

Agent MUST NOT produce ANY of these in output OR conversation.

### Subject Line
- `RE:`, `Re:`, `re:`, `FW:`, `Fw:`, `fw:`, `Fwd:`, `fwd:`
- Em-dashes / hyphens as delimiters: `WSR - {date} - {project}`
- Commas / semicolons as delimiters
- Anything BEFORE `WSR |`

### Section Headers
- `Project Update:` (must be `Summary of WSR:`)
- `Summary: TBD`
- `Summary:` (missing "of WSR" suffix)
- `Status:` without hyphen (must be `Status -`)

### Metric Names (Zero Tolerance)
- `Capacity Utilization` (American) → must be `Capacity Utilisation`
- `Capacity Util` / `Cap Util` abbreviations
- `User Stories Delivered` (plural) → must be `User Story Delivered`
- `Story Delivered` / `US Delivered` → must be full phrase
- `Defects Per Days: 2.5%` → decimal only, no `%`
- `Defects/Day` / `Defect Per Day` / `DpD%`

### Placeholder Tokens
- `TBD`, `To be determined`, `[insert here]`, `<value>`, `XX%` without real value
- Blank/empty section content

### Sycophantic / Autopilot Openers
- *"Great job!"*, *"This looks perfect!"*, *"Excellent work!"*
- *"You're absolutely right!"* — never validate without evidence
- *"I'll proceed assuming..."*, *"Meanwhile, let me..."*, *"Since you said proceed, I'll..."*

### v1.1 Anti-Patterns (NEW)
- *"What date should I use?"* — Date is auto-injected, never ask
- *"What's your project name?"* (when reference provides it) — Use `[from reference]` instead
- *"Let me ask you about each section one by one"* — Single batch only
- Any per-section "approve to continue" prompt — Approval happens once at SP2

