## COMPLIANCE SELF-CHECK (Run Before Each Stop Point)

### Before SP1 (Phase 1 batch presentation)
```
☐ Mode detected (A or B) and stored in state
☐ Today's date auto-injected (NOT asked)
☐ All 5 subject components either [from reference] or asked in batch
☐ All 6 sections rendered (inferred or skeletal with MISSING markers)
☐ Leaves prompt included
☐ Jira-paste prompt included
☐ Free-form prompt included
☐ Bidirectional sycophancy nudge included if applicable
☐ Inferred fields marked [from reference]
☐ Missing fields marked ⚠️ MISSING
☐ Single message — NOT split into multiple prompts
```

### Before SP2 (Phase 2 final draft presentation)
```
☐ User's batch reply parsed (leaves dict, Jira → metrics dict, freeform, section edits) — LLM-native parse
☐ Days computed via days_calculator.py
☐ Metrics computed via metrics_calculator.py
☐ Bidirectional sycophancy re-check applied to updated state
☐ All 6 validators executed silently
☐ LLM <thinking> self-checks: date is dd-mmm-yy, recipient = gdc-project-collaboration@salesforce.com,
   no Re:/Fw: in subject, all 6 sections in correct order, no forbidden headers (Project Update:, Summary: TBD)
☐ Auto-fixes applied where safe (Utilization → Utilisation, decimals)
☐ Critical FAILs surfaced with specific remediation ask
☐ Subject line matches subject_regex
☐ All 6 body sections in exact order (silent body_structure_validator)
☐ 4 bundle files written: subject.txt + email_body.html + validation_report.md + run_metadata.json
☐ Bundle folder uses {YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm}_{project-slug} pattern
☐ Inline plain-text preview rendered in chat (NOT to file)
☐ Inline gap list rendered in chat (NOT to file) AND captured in run_metadata.json gaps[]
☐ Open-in-browser send instructions displayed (HTML→Gmail flow)
☐ Recipients include gdc-project-collaboration@salesforce.com
```

